{
  "_comment": [
    "Chart of accounts, QuickBooks-style. code -> name, type, detail, entity, schedule_c.",
    "type drives everything downstream: Income -> counts as income, Expense/COGS -> counts as",
    "expense, Asset/Liability/Equity -> transfer, which never touches a total. That is why a",
    "card payment (Liability 2010) and an ATM pull (Asset 1090) are automatically neutral.",
    "schedule_c lives HERE, not on the vendor rule, so changing a line changes it everywhere.",
    "Numbering: 1000 asset, 2000 liability, 3000 equity, 4000 income, 5000 COGS, 6000 business",
    "expense, 7000 personal expense. x990 is the parking lot for each block, kept visible on",
    "purpose so 'uncategorized' can never hide inside a real account."
  ],

